hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1209","Yaqoub bin Ibrahim Al-Dawraqi told us, Ali bin Al-Hasan bin Shaqiq told us, Al-Hussein bin Waqid told us, Abdullah bin Buraidah, on the authority of his father, said: One morning the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, called Bilal and said: “O Bilal! Why did you race me to Paradise?” Yesterday, I entered Paradise and heard your rattle in front of me.” Bilal said: O Messenger of God, I have never sinned except that I prayed two rak’ahs, and I did not sin. Never had an incident happen to me without me performing ablution then, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “With this.”"
